{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"OVERLAP WITH c2ba-98bf-ca2d-481a (rewrite of a lost \"--body\" comment).\n\nc2ba (filed from 1a47) independently proved that src/rebar/_store/event_append.py runs its lock-held\n`git add`/`git commit` with NO timeout= (unlike push.py). That is the SAME site this ticket lists,\nnow with a RUNTIME PROOF attached rather than a static sweep — treat c2ba's evidence as input here.\n\nc2ba's other half is BROADER than this ticket and NOT covered by it: review_bot/voter.py calls the\nsynchronous emit_code_review_artifact directly on the event loop. Measured: shutdown took 3.00s\nagainst a declared 0.2s bound, and a 0.1s heartbeat showed a single 2.01s gap. Consequence: the\ndrain's wait_for cannot fire, cancel() cannot be delivered, and `await task` is unbounded — so the\nworst-case store write is NOT COMPUTABLE, and the 150s stop_grace_period shipped under 1a47 is a\nlarge risk reduction rather than a proof.\n\nClosing c2ba means changing the production review path's CONCURRENCY MODEL — a design decision, not\na timeout value. The OSS research commissioned for this ticket should inform BOTH. Do not settle\nc2ba's concurrency question before those findings land."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785543545398814001,"uuid":"76496612-a09a-481f-9f7d-3c290955e03a"}